# NEAR-KICKOFF-CAPTURE, Epicbet third, on the VPS (2026-09-22).
#
# `near_kickoff_capture` snaps closing prices for fixtures inside T-15min at the
# three direct books. It ran wholly on the Mac because two of the three
# transports only existed there. Epicbet is not one of them: with the residential
# egress the VPS reaches it with plain requests, ~0.7s for the full category
# listing, and FlareSolverr is never opened.
#
# (Historical, pre-2026-09-23: the Mac ran the other books; its plist is now parked.)
# Was: THE MAC STILL RUNS THE OTHER TWO. Its plist must be `--books
# Coolbet,Unibet-Site`. If both sides run Epicbet the writes are not duplicated
# (MIN_GAP_MIN skips a (match, book) priced in the last 6 minutes) but the two
# jobs race for the same window and the Mac pays FlareSolverr cost for nothing.
# Check: grep -A12 ProgramArguments ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.oddsintel.near-kickoff-capture.plist
#
# Timer, not a loop: every 5 minutes, matching the Mac's StartInterval.

[Unit]
Description=OddsIntel near-kickoff capture (Epicbet + Coolbet + Unibet-Site, via Estonian egress)
After=network-online.target
Wants=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=oneshot
User=root
WorkingDirectory=/opt/odds-intel-engine
EnvironmentFile=/opt/odds-intel-engine/.env
Environment=TZ=UTC
Environment=PYTHONUNBUFFERED=1
# ZONE-EGRESS 2026-09-23: was socks5h://10.8.0.2:1080, the WireGuard tunnel to
# the operator's MacBook. Now the zone.ee exit node (AS49604, Tallinn), which
# does the same job without depending on a laptop being awake. Measured: an
# Estonian HOSTING ip is classified like an Estonian eyeball ip — Epicbet goes
# CF-CHALLENGE -> OK. socks5h so DNS resolves at the exit, not here.
Environment=EPICBET_RESIDENTIAL_PROXY=socks5h://127.0.0.1:1081
# COOLBET-NEAR-KICKOFF-MOVED 2026-09-23 — the Coolbet third follows the sweep
# onto the VPS. NOTE: deliberately NOT setting COOLBET_NO_FS here. The Mac ran
# it with NO_FS=1, which uses Imperva cookies loaded from the DB — harvested on
# the operator's own machine. Replaying those from the Estonian exit is the
# TLS-bound-token blackhole that made the first Coolbet cutover hang for 30s a
# call. Without NO_FS it uses the FlareSolverr path, which mints its own
# identity on this egress and is the one proven working.
Environment=COOLBET_RESIDENTIAL_PROXY=socks5h://127.0.0.1:1081
# Its own FS session id is now moot (FS is disabled when proxied) but kept so a
# fallback run without the proxy still cannot touch the sweep's session.
# CORRECTED 2026-09-23 (COOLBET-NEARKO-NO-FS-403): the note above said NO_FS is
# not set here — but capture_coolbet FORCED it in code, so the Coolbet close
# replayed Mac cookies and got 403 on every call. It now forces NO_FS only when
# no residential proxy is configured; on this box it uses the proxied FS path.
Environment=EPICBET_FLARE_SESSION=epicbet_nearko_reader
# UNIBET-ON-VPS 2026-09-23 — the Unibet-Site third joins. It reads the logged-OUT
# tab in oddsintel-unibet-chrome.service via UNIBET_CHROME_CDP_URL (from .env);
# capture_unibet never logs in. The Mac's near-kickoff-capture plist is parked,
# so all three books now close here. (Unit name kept for continuity.)
# TONYBET 2026-09-23 (#101 phase 1b): full-board close by stored event id.
ExecStart=/opt/odds-intel-engine/venv/bin/python -m workers.jobs.near_kickoff_capture --books Epicbet,Coolbet,Unibet-Site,Tonybet
